      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "The stuff on VRChat servers is not what I'd call original files, it's processed into unity asset bundles. To get that back into the editor, basically gotta rip it.\n\nWith all the complaints about how easy it is to rip from VRChat, if VRChat helps people rip thier own stuff, I think it'll be a contentionous move.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2024-01-24T14:03:09.423Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "|VRChat has just celebrated its 10 year anniversary, that is an entire decade and in that time we have had a lot of people upload worlds and avatars, this has led to a small issue, over time people lose access to there original files, hard drive crashes, lost files when transferring to a new computer or in some cases just plain accidental deletion.\n\nNow the problem with losing access to the original files is that when VRChat updates itself these older worlds and avatars can not be updated anymore,  we are losing a lot of worlds and avatars because of file loss.\n\nYet there is a place where the files are stored and that is VRChat itself, they hold the original files on there servers.\n\nIs this possible, is there a way for VRChat to allow world creators and avatar creators to export there worlds and avatars back out of VRChat in the case they lose them?\n\nOr a way in Unity to open new project and export the world/avatar back into unity that you can then save a copy off.\n\nThis would enable so many worlds and avatars to be upgraded and save them from obsolescence.\n\nNow we do not want to risk a compromised account giving access to all the worlds and avatars uploaded so I would also recommend you need to turn on 2FA to enable this exporting mode.\n\nHope this is considered there are a lot of people who would love to get access to there lost worlds and avatars again.",
